# Application metadata and service transport. Editor behavior lives in dynlex-ui.
import configuration.dl
import theme.dl

to [open website source editors in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set instance to state's view's instance
    set state's language to a UI source workspace in instance rooted at "file:///workspace"
    enable UI source tools for (state's language) in (state's view)
    configure the website shader source named "shader.dl" in state
    set description to the item at (the website program for source "River source") in (the website program descriptions)
    configure the website source editor "River source" named (the string form of (description's filename)) prefixed by (the string form of (description's prefix)) using UI CPU analysis in state
    set river to the UI source editor labeled "River source" in (state's language)
    set river's diagnostics to the control labeled "River analysis diagnostics" in instance
    set river's status to the control labeled "River analysis" in instance
    set river's clean text to ""
    set river's ready text to "Plan checked"
    set description to the item at (the website program for source "Farm source") in (the website program descriptions)
    configure the website source editor "Farm source" named (the string form of (description's filename)) prefixed by (the string form of (description's prefix)) using UI CPU analysis in state
    set farm to the UI source editor labeled "Farm source" in (state's language)
    set farm's diagnostics to the control labeled "Farm analysis diagnostics" in instance
    set farm's status to the control labeled "Farm analysis" in instance
    set farm's clean text to ""
    set farm's ready text to "Role checked"
    set labels to ["IDE source", "Shader source"]
    set index to 0
    loop while index < the length of labels:
        set editor to the UI source editor labeled (the item at index in labels) in (state's language)
        set editor's diagnostics to the control labeled "IDE diagnostics" in instance
        set editor's status to the control labeled "IDE analysis" in instance
        increment index

to [send website language work] {UI language work:work} [in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    if work's step != 0:
        request "language" containing (work's payload) for purpose 8 indexed (work's step) in state

to [receive website language reply] {a pointer to JSON value:response} [at step] {integer:step} [in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    synchronize UI source workspace (state's language) at (state's view's seconds) seconds
    send website language work (the UI language reply response at step step in (state's language's client)) in state
    present website source colors in state
    animate UI view (state's view)

to [advance website language analysis in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set view to state's view
    update UI source tools in (state's language)
    set work to the next UI source workspace work in (state's language) focused on (the UI source focus in view for (state's language)) at (view's seconds) seconds
    send website language work work in state
    present website source colors in state
    if UI source workspace (state's language) awaits an edit deadline at (view's seconds) seconds:
        animate UI view view

to [notice website source edit] {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set state to the website state in instance
    if the website editor uses shaders in state:
        if state's shader editor's source request != 0:
            ignore cancel website request (state's shader editor's source request) in state
            set state's shader editor's source request to 0
        set state's shader editor's source failed to false
        set the text of "Run program ▶" in instance to "Recompile shader ↻"
    synchronize UI source workspace (state's language) at (state's view's seconds) seconds
    animate UI view (state's view)
